.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 43% operating margin runs 35pp above the Consumer Defensive median (7%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It captures 5.27x its revenue share in sector profits, taking a disproportionate slice of the profit pool.","It accounts for 0.7% of sector revenue and 3.7% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-5.3% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.07 across 172 companies in the universe; the top four hold 38% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 28% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the top of its 52-week range, 5% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 25% and a beta of 0.28, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.57 vs 5y 0.16), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $549.5M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 39% in the 2020 crash, 26% in the 2022 bear market and 38% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 34% below its DCF fair value of $116, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 5%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $82.40 to $172 (P10-P90).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 163% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 7.2% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $73.45 on average, 4% below the price, well away from the model's fair value.","The price implies 2.9% annual cash-flow growth, 8pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 46% clears the cost of capital of 6.0% by 40pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.28).","It runs a 47% gross margin and converts 39% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.34x.","It spends 0.8% of revenue on R&D."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.1x net debt to EBITDA ($4.5B of cash against $25.7B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 8.4x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 4.9, in the safe zone).","The current ratio of 0.65 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -2.5% over 3 years, -2.3% over 5 years and -0.9% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 14% of profits supports about 6.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 2.2% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.2% trend).","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.8x, 0.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Analysts expect 3.9% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 65%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 3 sales over the past year, net $2.3M sold.","It returns 6.3% a year to shareholders (0.8% in buybacks and 5.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 64 consecutive years, raising it 2.0% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 5,900 employees, each generates about $3.9M of revenue, 7.8x the Consumer Defensive median.","That works out to $1.5M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.6M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":77,"head":"Invest: trades 34% below fair value of $116; ROIC 45.6% vs WACC 6.0%.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 60, gates 15/25)","Trades 34% below fair value of $116","ROIC 45.6% vs WACC 6.0%","FCF margin 39.0%","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Revenue shrank 2.3%/yr over 5y"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":98.51,"vc":{"base":115.9,"base_src":"dcf","bear":82.4,"bull":171.8,"alt_median":134.26,"n_alt":2,"gap":-0.0572,"dispersion":0.0544,"